  "body": "**What happens:** with a model and a tool but no stock, every create cell (for example **Milling 2D → Face**) can be clicked. The click then refuses with \"no stock; set up stock first\", shown on a status line that's hard to read (see the companion issue). The ribbon already disables create cells when there's no tool; there's no equivalent for \"no stock\".\n\n**Expected:** create cells whose default heights need stock are disabled until stock exists, with a hover tooltip saying why (\"set up stock first\"). Or the click opens the Stock page. Either way, the user isn't left with a silent no-op.\n\nSuggested labels: `enhancement`, `P2`, `area:ui`, `source:agent`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
